{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need to book a table at Dishoom Canary Wharf?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Book anytime before 6pm. After 6pm, bookings are open for groups of 6+. If your desired time isn’t available, simply come along – we keep most of our tables for walk-ins."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What time is breakfast and brunch served in Dishoom Canary Wharf?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Breakfast is served Monday to Friday from 8am – 11.45am and Saturday to Sunday from 9am – 11.45am. The All Day menu is served from 12pm daily for delicious lunches, afternoon snacks, dinner and late-night tipples."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I book semi-private group dining spaces at Dishoom Canary Wharf?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, we have three semi-private dining spaces groups both small and large, well-suited for breakfast meetings, client lunches or company milestones worthy of granduer. All are warmly welcomed, while tables are laden with café favourites from our Breakfast Feast and Group Feast menus (non-veg., veg. and vegan options for all). For Group Bookings: simply enquire here."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Dishoom Canary Wharf have outdoor seating?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, all cafés (except Dishoom Kensington and Manchester) open out into the air* for patrons to feast under fresh skies. Bask in the best of sunnier days, or bring character to your lunch with a playful breeze or bluster. Indeed, everything tastes better outside…

Passersby may also wish to pop into Dishoom Shoreditch’s indoor-outdoor Verandah, flooded with daylight, sensibly sheltered and suitably warm for year-round delight.

*Kindly note:— due to the vagaries of weather, it is not possible to book our outdoor tables. When warmer months greet us, simply ask for a table outside upon arrival. We’ll do our best to accommodate."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I make a booking for my birthday at Dishoom Canary Wharf?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, extra-special reservations are met with abundant joy – tell us it's a celebration when you book, and let your server know on arrival. If your party is for 6 or more, make a Group Booking for a big-hearted celebration, with the choice of a semi-private dining space, seating 26–32 guests.. Sip on finest tipples and teetotals while tables are flooded with café favourites from our Group Feast menus (non veg., veg. and vegan options for all). Simply enquire here."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Dishoom Canary Wharf vegetarian, vegan and gluten-free friendly? ","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, our All Day menu is filled with much-loved vegetarian dishes, including Pau Bhaji, Makhmali Paneer, House Black Daal and Gunpowder Potatoes. We also have a dedicated vegan and gluten-free menu available. All diets are happily fed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Dishoom Canary Wharf halal-friendly? ","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, all dishes on the All Day menu are halal-friendly. Pick freely. On the Breakfast menu, dishes that contain bacon or pork sausages are not halal. Plenty of options remain: cooked breakfasts, egg naan rolls and fresh fruits & grains. Do ask your server if you have any questions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long is the queue at Dishoom Canary Wharf?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"At breakfast and lunchtime, walk right in – there will be little or no queue. After 6pm and on weekends, a queue gathers around the café at busier times. You’ll be refreshed with complimentary chai while you wait, and as soon as space allows, can take a seat at the bar with tipples and snacks while your table is readied. Total wait times can range from 30 minutes to 1 hour."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I get to Dishoom Canary Wharf?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The entrance to Dishoom Canary Wharf is located on Water Street, in Wood Wharf. It is a short walk from Canary Wharf Underground station (around 5 minutes) on the Jubilee line. The nearest Bus Stops are Water Street / Wood Wharf (Stops A and B), both a 1–2 minute walk away."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Dishoom Canary Wharf wheelchair accessible?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, Dishoom Canary Wharf is wheelchair accessible, with a step-free entrance, accessible seating and a disabled loo. For any access needs, please phone ahead if you have any queries – we’re happy to help."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should I order at Dishoom Canary Wharf?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Dip into our menus. Beloved morning dishes include Breakfast Naan Rolls, Akuri Pau and Date & Banana Porridge. At lunch: Vada Pau, generously filled khati rolls, Dishoom House Chaat and Chilli Broccoli Salad. At dinner, feast: crisp samosas, Dishoom Chicken Ruby, Chef’s Special Salli Boti and House Black Daal."}}]}
